  "term": "CSA",
  "definition": "CSA, or central sleep apnea, is a sleep-related breathing problem in which breathing repeatedly stops during sleep because the brain’s breathing center responds less to carbon dioxide. This leads to alternating periods of stopped breathing and overbreathing.",
